<title>ROMANIA: Romania 10-month current account gap $1.074 bln.</title>
<headline>Romania 10-month current account gap $1.074 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's current account deficit climbed to $1.074 billion in January-October from $713 million in January-September, but was lower than a $1.13 billion gap in the same 1995 period, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Latest statistics put Romania's trade deficit at $1.17 billion in January-November 1996, but that does not include November oil imports. These, together with December imports, are expected to take the 1996 trade deficit to $2.0 billion, according to local economists.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN CURRENT A/C	  JAN-OCT 96	   JAN-OCT 95</p>
<p> Current account (million USD)    -1,074		   -1,136</p>
<p> Trade balance		    -1,043		   -1,140</p>
<p> Exports (FOB)		     6,061		    6,457</p>
<p> Imports (FOB)		     7,104		    7,597</p>
<p> Services balance		    -90			-10</p>
<p> Income balance		     -242		     -189</p>
<p> Current transfers balance	 301			203</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
